4, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -0.78}, "rating_margin": -15.3, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.16, "baseline_margin": -10.33, "analyst_adjustment": -0.17, "key_factors": ["District's R+8 partisan lean and Harris's incumbency advantage", "Consensus of expert raters at Solid/Safe R", "Harris's large fundraising and cash edge over Schwartz", "Redistricting headlines raised risk, but courts upheld the map"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Republican hold: an R+8 district, a well-funded incumbent, and a July poll showing Harris up 13. Redistricting chatter briefly threatened the seat, but the Maryland Supreme Court upheld the Democratic map without moving MD-01, and markets price Harris near 89%.", "watch": "Any late-breaking change to the congressional map or a surge of Democratic outside spending could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 66 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Andy Harris (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Andy Harris seeks another term in Maryland's Eastern Shore district, which leans Republican by about eight points. He enters the general election with a large financial advantage, having raised $2.3 million and holding $1.85 million on hand, while Democrat Dan Schwartz has raised under $700,000 with limited cash remaining. A July live-caller poll showed Harris ahead 52-39, and prediction markets give him roughly an 89% chance of winning.\n\nThe race drew attention over the summer when a Democratic redistricting effort threatened to make the seat more competitive, but the Maryland Supreme Court upheld the existing map in early September, leaving the district's boundaries intact. Expert raters across the spectrum place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and the fundamentals model points to a double-digit Republican margin. Schwartz remains a long shot, though Harris's polarizing profile and the district's shifting demographics give Democrats a narrow path if the national environment breaks sharply their way.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1047, "margin": -9.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0918, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0624, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0531, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0618, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.101, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0704, "margin": -10.5}]}